<%--
Password_Input - one password field

A form input like any other - ONE named value, the text typed. The framework's own forms
that ask for a password (<Password_Confirmation_Form>) use it, so they need no application
input component.

    <Password_Input $name="password" />

$name          - the field name (form contract).
$autocomplete  - the browser hint; 'current-password' unless given ('new-password' for a
                 password being chosen).
$placeholder   - optional placeholder text.

The field is a Bootstrap .form-control, so its look is the application's own.
--%>
<Define:Password_Input extends="Form_Input_Abstract" tag="div">
    <input type="password" class="form-control" $sid="field"
           autocomplete="<%= this.args.autocomplete || 'current-password' %>"
           <% if (this.args.placeholder) { %>placeholder="<%= this.args.placeholder %>"<% } %> />
</Define:Password_Input>
